WHY THE AGPL

This is not an arbitrary choice. The app renders and edits PDFs with PyMuPDF,
which Artifex dual-licenses as AGPL-3.0 or under a paid commercial licence.
Distributing a build that contains PyMuPDF means the combined work must be
offered under the AGPL as well, unless a commercial licence for PyMuPDF has been
bought from Artifex.

If that is not what you want, there are two ways out, and both are real work:

  * Buy a commercial PyMuPDF licence from Artifex, after which this project can
    be relicensed however you like.
  * Replace PyMuPDF with a permissively licensed PDF library. pypdfium2
    (Apache-2.0/BSD-3-Clause) is the usual candidate, but it does not offer the
    redaction API this app relies on to remove the original text, so the
    renderer would have to be rewritten.

See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md for every other dependency and its licence.

